# Welcome {hideTitle}

## Welcome

This module combines explainers, interaction, and quick decision points.

::: accordion {style=shaded}
:: Hazard Types
Physical hazards include slips, noise, and moving machinery.

:: Procedural hazards
Procedural hazards include skipped checks and unclear handoffs.

:: Reporting hazards
Report hazards immediately and include location plus severity.
:::

::: tabs {style=pills orientation=vertical}
:: Before Shift
Review overnight incidents and pending actions.

:: During Shift
Use the checklist and escalate unresolved hazards.
:::

::: columns
::
### Risks

- Chemical splash
- Electrical fault
- Fall from ladder

::
### Controls

- Face shield and gloves
- Lockout/tagout
- Guard rail and harness
:::

::: video /assets/lab-safety-walkthrough.mp4 {captions=/assets/lab-safety-walkthrough.en.vtt start=12 end=90}
caption: Lab safety walkthrough
:::

::: note {tone=note style=shaded}
Use the buddy system for high-risk tasks.
:::

::: note {tone=warning style=outline}
Stop work immediately when controls fail.
:::

::: checklist {required}
- [ ] Inspect exits
- [ ] Confirm PPE
- [ ] Review incident board
:::

::: button [Open Full SOP](https://example.com/sop) {style=outline newTab}
:::

::: choice Decision Scenario {points=5}
A solvent leak appears near a heat source. Choose the safest first response.
(x) Shut off the heat source and contain the spill
feedback: Correct. Eliminate the ignition source first, then contain.
( ) Evacuate immediately without containment
feedback: Evacuation may be needed, but containment prevents escalation.
:::

